msgstr "Cell di bawah ini mengimpor alat yang dibutuhkan dan mendefinisikan fungsi bantu yang dipakai untuk menganalisis hasil. Fungsi yang membangun circuit didefinisikan langkah demi langkah di contoh skala kecil di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each circuit stores its measurement outcomes in up to four classical registers:\n"
msgstr "Setiap circuit menyimpan hasil pengukurannya dalam hingga empat register klasik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`fusion`: the parity measurements used to fuse the GHZ patches\n"
msgstr "`fusion`: pengukuran paritas yang dipakai untuk menggabungkan patch GHZ\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`ghz`: the GHZ readout bits that herald the W state (the root of each pair, or every GHZ qubit with no error detection)\n"
msgstr "`ghz`: bit pembacaan GHZ yang menandai state W (root dari tiap pasangan, atau setiap qubit GHZ jika tanpa deteksi error)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`flag`: the DisCo ED check bits (one per pair; not present without error detection)\n"
msgstr "`flag`: bit pemeriksaan DisCo ED (satu per pasangan; tidak ada tanpa deteksi error)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`w`: the final measurement of the W qubits\n"
msgstr "`w`: pengukuran akhir qubit W\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The analysis has three steps. `postselect` keeps only the shots that pass the DisCo ED check (`flag` is cross-checked with `ghz`) and that herald the odd-parity sector (an odd number of 1s in `ghz`). The kept `w` bits then give the Hamming-weight distribution, the coherence $C$, and bounds on the fidelity $F$ with $|W_n\\rangle$. Finally, `exact_reference` gives the ideal values derived in the Background section. (If the circuits were built with `feedforward=False`, `postselect` first applies the GHZ corrections that were left for postprocessing. See Step 1 below.)\n"
msgstr "Analisisnya punya tiga langkah. `postselect` hanya menyimpan shot yang lolos pemeriksaan DisCo ED (`flag` dicek silang dengan `ghz`) dan yang menandai sektor paritas ganjil (jumlah 1 yang ganjil di `ghz`). Bit `w` yang disimpan kemudian memberi distribusi bobot Hamming, koherensi $C$, dan batas fidelity $F$ terhadap $|W_n\\rangle$. Terakhir, `exact_reference` memberi nilai ideal yang diturunkan di bagian Latar belakang. (Kalau circuit dibangun dengan `feedforward=False`, `postselect` lebih dulu menerapkan koreksi GHZ yang ditinggalkan untuk pasca-pemrosesan. Lihat Langkah 1 di bawah.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator skala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, run the protocol in simulation for $n = 6$ W qubits (12 qubits in total), in two ways:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, jalankan protokol dalam simulasi untuk $n = 6$ qubit W (12 qubit secara total), dengan dua cara:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Expected reference:** the ideal values derived in the Background section, computed by `exact_reference`. `StatevectorSampler` cannot run circuits that contain classical feedforward (`if_test`), so this example also runs the logical (untranspiled) circuits on the noiseless `AerSimulator`. This checks both the circuits and the postprocessing: without noise, every shot should pass the DisCo ED check, and the results should agree with the expected values up to shot noise.\n"
msgstr "**Referensi yang diharapkan:** nilai ideal yang diturunkan di bagian Background, dihitung oleh `exact_reference`. `StatevectorSampler` tidak bisa menjalankan circuit yang berisi feedforward klasik (`if_test`), jadi contoh ini juga menjalankan circuit logis (yang belum di-transpile) di `AerSimulator` tanpa noise. Ini memeriksa circuit sekaligus postprocessing-nya: tanpa noise, setiap shot seharusnya lolos pemeriksaan DisCo ED, dan hasilnya harus cocok dengan nilai yang diharapkan sampai batas shot noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Noisy run:** [local testing mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) with `FakeMiami`, a fake Nighthawk backend with the same square lattice as the hardware example. This shows how far a hardware-like result drifts from the expected one, and how much of the gap DisCo ED recovers.\n"
msgstr "**Run dengan noise:** [mode pengujian lokal](/guides/local-testing-mode) dengan `FakeMiami`, backend Nighthawk tiruan dengan kisi persegi yang sama seperti contoh di hardware. Ini menunjukkan seberapa jauh hasil mirip hardware menyimpang dari hasil yang diharapkan, dan seberapa besar selisih yang bisa dipulihkan DisCo ED.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit uses two lines of $n$ qubits: the GHZ line `q_ghz`, which serves as the distributed control, and the W line `q_w`, which ends up in the W state. The circuit has three pieces, one for each stage of the protocol.\n"
msgstr "Circuit ini memakai dua baris berisi $n$ qubit: baris GHZ `q_ghz`, yang berfungsi sebagai kontrol terdistribusi, dan baris W `q_w`, yang akhirnya berada dalam state W. Circuit ini punya tiga bagian, satu untuk tiap tahap protokol.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**1. Prepare the GHZ state.** `prepare_ghz` splits the GHZ line into the staggered patches $[0], [1, 2], [3, 4], \\ldots$ (the last patch also takes the final qubit) and prepares a small GHZ state in each patch. It then fuses neighboring patches. A CNOT copies the parity $Z_aZ_b$ of the two qubits on either side of a boundary onto $b$, the first qubit of the right patch. Qubit $b$ is then measured into `fusion`, reset, and re-entangled with its patch. Finally, the feedforward applies $X$ to every qubit of patch $k$ if the parity of the first $k$ fusion outcomes is odd. The conditions are built with `expr.bit_xor`, so all corrections happen in one round of feedforward.\n"
msgstr "**1. Siapkan state GHZ.** `prepare_ghz` membagi baris GHZ menjadi patch berselang-seling $[0], [1, 2], [3, 4], \\ldots$ (patch terakhir juga mengambil qubit terakhir) dan menyiapkan state GHZ kecil di tiap patch. Lalu patch yang bertetangga digabungkan. Sebuah CNOT menyalin paritas $Z_aZ_b$ dari dua qubit di kedua sisi batas ke $b$, qubit pertama dari patch kanan. Qubit $b$ kemudian diukur ke `fusion`, di-reset, dan dientangle ulang dengan patch-nya. Terakhir, feedforward menerapkan $X$ ke setiap qubit patch $k$ jika paritas dari $k$ hasil fusion pertama ganjil. Kondisinya dibangun dengan `expr.bit_xor`, sehingga semua koreksi terjadi dalam satu putaran feedforward.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every correction is an $X$, and the rest of the circuit only moves it around: the CZ layer turns $X_{g_j}$ into $X_{g_j}Z_{w_j}$, and the GHZ readout carries it onto known bits. So the measurement statistics are the same if, instead of applying the corrections on the device, you apply them to the measured bits afterward (`deferred_corrections` and `postselect` in the Setup cell). This is called tracking the *Pauli frame*. Note that it does not prepare the W state on the device; it only reproduces the outcomes that the device would have measured. `prepare_ghz` therefore applies the corrections in real time by default (`feedforward=True`). Setting `feedforward=False` is a useful diagnostic: it removes the wait for the fusion outcomes to reach the controller and come back, during which the whole GHZ line idles, so comparing the two settings shows how much error that wait adds.\n"
msgstr "Setiap koreksi adalah sebuah $X$, dan sisa circuit hanya memindahkannya: layer CZ mengubah $X_{g_j}$ menjadi $X_{g_j}Z_{w_j}$, dan pembacaan GHZ membawanya ke bit yang diketahui. Jadi statistik pengukuran sama saja jika, alih-alih menerapkan koreksi di perangkat, kamu menerapkannya ke bit hasil ukur sesudahnya (`deferred_corrections` dan `postselect` di sel Setup). Ini disebut melacak *Pauli frame*. Perhatikan bahwa cara ini tidak menyiapkan state W di perangkat; ia hanya mereproduksi hasil yang akan diukur perangkat. Karena itu `prepare_ghz` menerapkan koreksi secara real time secara default (`feedforward=True`). Mengatur `feedforward=False` berguna sebagai diagnostik: ini menghilangkan waktu tunggu hingga hasil fusion sampai ke controller dan kembali, yang selama itu seluruh baris GHZ menganggur, jadi membandingkan kedua pengaturan menunjukkan seberapa besar error yang ditambahkan oleh waktu tunggu itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**2. Seed and couple the W qubits.** `couple_w_qubits` rotates every W qubit with $R_Y(\\theta)$, where $\\theta = 2\\arcsin\\sqrt{\\delta/n}$ so that $p = \\delta/n$. It then applies $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ on every rung of the ladder, which is the controlled-$Z^{\\otimes n}$ of the distributed Hadamard test. The circuit applies the rotations after the GHZ preparation, just before the CZ layer. That way, the W qubits wait in $|0\\rangle$, which does not decay, during the slow mid-circuit measurements and feedforward.\n"
msgstr "**2. Seed dan kopel qubit W.** `couple_w_qubits` merotasi setiap qubit W dengan $R_Y(\\theta)$, dengan $\\theta = 2\\arcsin\\sqrt{\\delta/n}$ sehingga $p = \\delta/n$. Lalu ia menerapkan $CZ(g_j, w_j)$ pada setiap anak tangga ladder, yaitu controlled-$Z^{\\otimes n}$ dari Hadamard test terdistribusi. Circuit menerapkan rotasi setelah persiapan GHZ, tepat sebelum layer CZ. Dengan begitu, qubit W menunggu dalam $|0\\rangle$, yang tidak meluruh, selama pengukuran mid-circuit yang lambat dan feedforward.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**3. Read out the GHZ state with DisCo ED.** `readout_ghz` measures the logical $\\bar X$ of the GHZ state. With `check=None`, every GHZ qubit is measured in the $X$ basis into `ghz`. With `\"explicit\"` or `\"implicit\"`, the GHZ line is split into the pairs $(2k, 2k+1)$, as described in the Background section. The root $r = 2k+1$ is measured into bit $k$ of `ghz`, and the check $c = 2k$ into bit $k$ of `flag`. The only difference between the two checks is the second CNOT.\n"
msgstr "**3. Baca state GHZ dengan DisCo ED.** `readout_ghz` mengukur $\\bar X$ logis dari state GHZ. Dengan `check=None`, setiap qubit GHZ diukur di basis $X$ ke `ghz`. Dengan `\"explicit\"` atau `\"implicit\"`, baris GHZ dibagi menjadi pasangan $(2k, 2k+1)$, seperti dijelaskan di bagian Background. Root $r = 2k+1$ diukur ke bit $k$ dari `ghz`, dan check $c = 2k$ ke bit $k$ dari `flag`. Satu-satunya perbedaan antara kedua check adalah CNOT kedua.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`build_w_state_circuit` puts the three pieces together, then measures the W qubits in the requested basis. The barriers only separate the stages in the circuit drawing.\n"
msgstr "`build_w_state_circuit` menyatukan ketiga bagian itu, lalu mengukur qubit W di basis yang diminta. Barrier hanya memisahkan tahap-tahap dalam gambar circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example builds nine circuits for $n = 6$: three DisCo ED modes, each measured in three bases. The $Z$-basis circuits give the Hamming-weight distribution, and the $X$- and $Y$-basis circuits give the coherence $C$. The cell below draws the implicit-check circuit with $Z$-basis measurements. From left to right, you can see the GHZ preparation, with its two fusion measurements and the feedforward corrections (`if_test` blocks); the rotations and the CZ rungs; and the paired DisCo ED readout. Note that the two-qubit depth of each stage does not depend on $n$.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini membangun sembilan circuit untuk $n = 6$: tiga mode DisCo ED, masing-masing diukur di tiga basis. Circuit basis $Z$ memberikan distribusi Hamming-weight, dan circuit basis $X$ dan $Y$ memberikan koherensi $C$. Sel di bawah menggambar circuit implicit-check dengan pengukuran basis $Z$. Dari kiri ke kanan, kamu bisa melihat persiapan GHZ, dengan dua pengukuran fusion dan koreksi feedforward (blok `if_test`); rotasi dan anak tangga CZ; dan pembacaan DisCo ED berpasangan. Perhatikan bahwa kedalaman dua-qubit tiap tahap tidak bergantung pada $n$.\n"

