#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware runs {#hardware-runs}"
msgstr "Run di hardware {#hardware-runs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–3: Map, optimize, and submit {#steps-13-map-optimize-and-submit}"
msgstr "Langkah 1–3: Petakan, optimalkan, dan kirim {#steps-13-map-optimize-and-submit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, put these steps together at a larger scale and submit the job to real quantum hardware. Prepare a W state on $n = 10$ qubits, using 20 qubits of `ibm_chicago`, a Nighthawk processor. The functions are the same as in the small-scale example; only $n$, $\\delta$, the backend, and the number of shots change. Because the protocol has constant depth, the transpiled circuits have the same CZ depth as for $n = 6$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, gabungkan langkah-langkah ini dalam skala lebih besar dan kirim job ke hardware kuantum asli. Siapkan state W pada $n = 10$ qubit, memakai 20 qubit dari `ibm_chicago`, prosesor Nighthawk. Fungsinya sama seperti di contoh skala kecil; hanya $n$, $\\delta$, backend, dan jumlah shot yang berubah. Karena protokolnya berkedalaman konstan, circuit hasil transpile punya kedalaman CZ yang sama seperti untuk $n = 6$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three settings matter on hardware:\n"
msgstr "Tiga pengaturan penting di hardware:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout.** `choose_layout` picks the 20 qubits from the current calibration, and all nine circuits run on them.\n"
msgstr "**Layout.** `choose_layout` memilih 20 qubit dari kalibrasi saat ini, dan kesembilan circuit berjalan di atasnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fast readout and dynamical decoupling.** `fast_readout` swaps in the device's faster measure and measure-and-reset instructions, and the GHZ line runs a dynamical decoupling sequence while the fusion qubits are measured.\n"
msgstr "**Fast readout dan dynamical decoupling.** `fast_readout` menukar instruksi measure dan measure-and-reset perangkat dengan yang lebih cepat, dan baris GHZ menjalankan urutan dynamical decoupling saat qubit fusion diukur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A larger $\\delta$.** On hardware, some even-parity shots pass the herald (see the DisCo ED section). Most of them have weight 0, and their size relative to the weight-1 component scales as $1/\\delta$. A larger $\\delta$ dilutes them, at the cost of more weight-3 contamination (about $\\delta^2/6$). This tutorial uses $\\delta = 0.6$, which gives an ideal fidelity of 0.95 and $r_s \\approx 0.36$.\n"
msgstr "**$\\delta$ yang lebih besar.** Di hardware, sebagian shot berparitas genap lolos herald (lihat bagian DisCo ED). Kebanyakan berbobot 0, dan ukurannya relatif terhadap komponen berbobot-1 berskala $1/\\delta$. $\\delta$ yang lebih besar mengencerkannya, dengan konsekuensi kontaminasi berbobot-3 yang lebih banyak (sekitar $\\delta^2/6$). Tutorial ini memakai $\\delta = 0.6$, yang memberi fidelity ideal 0.95 dan $r_s \\approx 0.36$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only a fraction of the shots are kept, so this run uses 20,000 shots per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Hanya sebagian shot yang dipertahankan, jadi run ini memakai 20.000 shot per circuit.\n"

